Fenrir wrote:

 > About exercising Dexterity... try disarming traps?

My personal favorite is "attempting to pick a lock",
since with some recent change, doing that with a
lock pick _always_ works, and works both ways lock
or unlock, so you can just keep picking a lock until
you have enough "lock picking" attempts to advance
your stat at the next checkpoint. You don't have to
take a step, the attempt is interruptible and so low
risk, your biggest worry is probably nutrition
consumption.

Granted, if you're losing dexterity, probably by
being satiated or strained, a unicorn horn will get
your stat back faster, but then exercising your stat
will advance the stat even more, and dexterity is a
good stat to advance.

xanthian.

I expect that being able to exercise dexterity
"forever" at a single door (or container) is an
exploit, so maybe there's some code somewhere that
disables doing that.



